+### Glue bit-identity (MK_CHECK had ~1e-6 relative mismatches on most elements of a glue output row)
+Cause: every replicated norm (glue, and the older CTRL_DOWN / CTRL_NORM / MIX fusions) computed the scale as
+`rsqrtf(__fadd_rn(sum / n, eps))` to keep an FMA out; but ggml-cuda compiles with `-use_fast_math`, so rms_norm_f32's
+`sum / n + eps` is a reciprocal multiplication contracted with the addition into one FMA, and the explicit add rounded
+once more. Same expression now, same contraction. Found with the self-test's new reference: `LLAMA_INKLING_MK_TEST`
+(set by the test at start-up) makes the backend read `LLAMA_INKLING_MK_REF` on every call, `=1` disables every fusion,
+so the glue cases compare against the truly unfused graph instead of the backend's own fusions (which hid the same
+error). New lines: `fused fusions: ...` (the backend's fusions vs unfused, with the controller intermediates h and out
+exposed to locate a differing one), `ref ... twice` (each path against itself), `-t <substring>` filter.
+Result: 68/69 PASS; the one FAIL left was the odd-state-count MIX (inexact against cuBLAS by design) and now compares
+against the fused reference. MK_CHECK in the server, every stage on, 300 decode steps: **0 mismatching** of 248640
+outputs (the diagnostic had a false mismatch of its own: the q8_1 slots are a ring that later shadow instances of the
+same declined run reuse; the bytes are copied out before the comparison now).
+
+### Why MK_MOE / MK_WO lost and glue2 trails glue
+- `mul_mat_vec_q_multi` / `_selfq` were 5-20% slower than `mul_mat_vec_q` on the same rows: the per-product arrays are
+  indexed with the block's matrix, and the compiler copied the whole parameter struct to local memory per thread
+  before indexing. `__grid_constant__` on the parameter fixes it (an unrolled select was tried first: worse). Self-test
+  after: moe gate_up nvfp4 39.1 -> 39.3 us, iq3_s 51.1 -> 52.4, q3_K 35.4 -> 37.2, down nvfp4 31.6 -> 33.2 (none
+  flagged, all still 1-5% slower per instance: MK_MOE has launch parity with the unfused path and a slightly slower
+  kernel, so it cannot win; with glue on, the unfused mmvq path takes the glue's q8_1 too). wo q8_0 19.3 -> 18.9 us.
+- glue2 (one cooperative kernel): 72 us vs 66 us per loop-pass instance for glue=1 in the self-test, 93 vs 95.7 tok/s.
+  The cooperative launch + grid barrier costs more than the launch it saves; per-unit completion tickets did not change
+  it. Kept as an experiment, not a default.
