+### Where the time went
+Decode profile (llama-bench tg48 under nsys, graphs on, `MK_GLUE=1`): the one-token Q8_0/Q6_K products are 2.18 ms
+of the ~10.9 ms per token, all plain `mul_mat_vec_q<type, 1, false>` launches (no fusion variant), 4 warps x 1 row per
+block. A plain read kernel (`scripts/inkling-gemv-bwprobe.cu`, 16-byte loads, no compute) sets the floor for a single
+kernel on this GPU: time = 1.3 us + bytes / 892 GB/s, i.e. 9.7 us for 7.5 MB (83% of 936 GB/s), 4.1 us for 2.5 MB
+(65%), 2.3 us for 0.94 MB (42%). **The 85% target is above that floor for every one of these shapes**; it would need
+the next kernel's loads to overlap this one's tail (PDL is Hopper+; cross-kernel L2 prefetch is a graph-level change).
+
+### What limits mul_mat_vec_q here, and the kernel
+Its K loop has a run-time trip count, so a thread issues the loads of iteration it+1 only after using those of
+iteration it: 3 dependent rounds of DRAM latency on 2304-wide Q8_0 rows. `inkling_gemv<type, ncols>` is the same
+kernel (same threads, the same `vec_dot_q8_0_q8_1` / `vec_dot_q6_K_q8_1` calls on the same slices, the same
+cross-warp and warp reduction) with ncols as a template parameter: the loop unrolls and all loads go out at once.
+Bit-identical by construction; dispatched only for (Q8_0 | Q6_K) x {2304 -> 3072, 1024, 384; 3072 -> 2304}, NVIDIA
+Ampere/Ada except Orin (mmvq's generic parameter table), weights not in a compute buffer; it takes the glue's q8_1 when
+there is one.
+
+Tried first and dropped (commit 553a43e6c has the first): staging the rows in shared memory to replace the 2-byte
+loads by 16-byte ones, bit-exact by recomputing mmvq's 128 per-thread partial sums from a conflict-free layout (pairs of
+blocks, 17 words, half warp per row) and reducing them in mmvq's order. Per-warp cp.async rings: 11.1 us; all loads in
+registers up front (one wave), then slice by slice through a shared-memory window: 11.15 us; 8 rows per block in one
+stage: 11.5 us (vs 11.65 for mmvq, 10.2 for the final kernel). Probes: without the compute the staging kernels took
+10.3-10.5 us, without the loads 5+ us: the computation from shared memory came after the last bytes arrived. The 2-byte
+loads are not the bottleneck on the 3090; the dependent load rounds are. More rows per block in the final kernel
+(2 or 4, sharing the activation loads) was slower too (11.0 / 11.0 us on 3072 rows).
+
+### Results (RTX 3090, evira)
+Per shape, kernel time in the decode graph (nsys, llama-bench tg48, `MK_GLUE=1`), before -> after; % of 936 GB/s:
+
+| type, shape (cols x rows) | calls/token | bytes | us before | us after | % before | % after | floor (plain read) | bit-identical |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| q8_0 2304 x 3072 (Q, gate) | 76 | 7.52 MB | 11.80 | 10.37 | 68% | 77% | 9.7 us | yes |
+| q8_0 3072 x 2304 (output) | 44 | 7.52 MB | 11.22 | 10.50 | 72% | 77% | 9.7 us | yes |
+| q8_0 2304 x 1024 (K, V) | 87 | 2.51 MB | 5.32 | 4.55 | 50% | 59% | 4.1 us | yes |
+| q8_0 2304 x 384 (R) | 34 | 0.94 MB | 3.28 | 2.95 | 31% | 34% | 2.3 us | yes |
+| q6_K 2304 x 3072 | 13 | 5.81 MB | 9.13 | 8.59 | 68% | 72% | 7.8 us | yes |
+| q6_K 3072 x 2304 | 4 | 5.81 MB | 8.93 | 8.65 | 69% | 72% | 7.8 us | yes |
+| q6_K 2304 x 1024 | 6 | 1.94 MB | 4.48 | 4.06 | 46% | 51% | 3.5 us | yes |
+| q6_K 2304 x 384 | 11 | 0.73 MB | 3.15 | 2.93 | 25% | 26% | 2.1 us | yes |
+
+Sum: 2.18 -> 1.95 ms per token (-232 us). test-inkling-gemv (random weights, 160 MB of copies per case so that L2
+does not help): 8/8 bit-identical to mul_mat_vec_q, NMSE vs a double-precision product 1.2-1.6e-5 for both.
+test-inkling-megakernel with `LLAMA_INKLING_GEMV=1`: 70/70 PASS (glue q8_1 consumed by the new kernel).
+
+mk-bench (`IMAGE=llamacpp-inkling2mini:gemv`, graphs on, 131072 ctx, greedy 512 tokens; short-1 / short-2 / after a
+54K prompt, tok/s):
