+| config | short-1 | short-2 | 54K |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| off | 90.5 | 90.6 | 72.1 |
+| gemv | 91.6 | 91.5 | 73.2 |
+| glue (round a / b) | 95.4 / 94.9 | 95.1 / 94.9 | 76.2 / 74.7 |
+| gemv + glue (round a / b) | 97.8 / 97.0 | 97.4 / 96.6 | 76.9 / 76.1 |
+
++2.0-2.5% short, +1-2% at 54K on top of `MK_GLUE=1` (+1.2% without glue). compare-quality (greedy top-10 over 128
+tokens): gemv+glue vs glue and gemv vs off both max |dp| 0, KL 0, 128/128 tokens the same, as bit identity implies.
+
+### Next
+The remaining gap to the floor is ~0.5 us per 7.5 MB product; past the floor only cross-kernel overlap helps: one
+launch for the 5 projections of a layer application (MK_PROJ's multi kernel with this unrolled body: the fixed
+1.3 us is paid once instead of 5 times, ~5 x 48 x 1 us = up to 0.25 ms/token), or the layer-application kernel.
+
+### Option A, steps 2-3 (committed c8474e171, b87a58dfa), the gemv merge (3e959ba0b)
+| step | what | MK_CHECK | mk-bench short / 54K | 
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 2 `LLAMA_INKLING_MK_MOESCALE=1` | the REPEAT + GET_ROWS of the per-expert scale table (2 launches per application) folded into upstream's fused MoE weighted reduction, which gathers the scale by the routed id and rounds every step as the unfused MUL/MUL/ADD do (upstream's `sum += (e*s)*w` contracts into an FMA, 1 ulp off the unfused graph; the switched variant is bit-identical to it) | 100-200 steps: 0 mismatching | glue+reltab 96.3-96.7 / 75.2-76.5 -> +moescale 96.7-97.3 / 75.8-76.4 (inside the noise); 1974 -> 1922 launched groups |
+| 3 SITU for the scale-less chain | the MK_DEBUG decline log showed the SITU fusion matching only 10 of 48 applications: the NVFP4 expert layers apply the scale inside the product kernel, so their chain has no MUL and neither matcher form fit; a third form (explicit subgraph indices: the gate/up views are not constants) fuses the 10 ops of the other 38 applications; always on | 100 steps: 0 mismatching | glue+reltab+moescale 96.7-97.3 / 75.8-76.4 -> 99.6-100.9 / 77.6-78.8 (+3%) |
