+
+Launch inventory after these: ~1920 groups per token (from 2078 with glue alone). The remaining barrier-free candidates
+(each ~0.5-1%): the gated wo input quantized in one kernel and handed to mmvq, SITU emitting the down product's q8_1
+(needs the hand-off to carry 8 rows), K/V clip + FWHT + SET_ROWS epilogues, Q clip + FWHT.
+
+### Option A, steps 4-5: `LLAMA_INKLING_MK_WOQ=1`, `LLAMA_INKLING_MK_QKV=1` (committed 58e91726e, matcher fix below)
+| step | what | MK_CHECK | mk-bench short / 54K |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 4 `LLAMA_INKLING_MK_WOQ=1` | the gated wo input (SIGMOID + MUL, 2 launches) quantized to q8_1 in one kernel and handed to the wo product through the glue's q8_1 slot ring, so the product skips its own quantize launch | 100 steps: 0 mismatching | rec 103.0-103.3 / 79.5-80.9 -> +woq 104.1-104.7 / 80.7 (+0.5-1%) |
+| 5 `LLAMA_INKLING_MK_QKV=1` | the Q/K/V epilogue of a token (Q clip with weight, optional tau, 128-wide Hadamard rotation; K clip, rotation; V RMS norm, 64-wide rotation; the two q8_0 cache stores: 14 launches) in one kernel of n_head + 2 n_kv blocks; the clips and norm are elementwise or one-warp reductions written as the unfused kernels, the rotation is `fwht_cuda`'s butterfly | 100 steps: 0 mismatching (117 792 outputs) | self-test 34 -> 17 us; see the fix below |
+
+QKV fired on 1 of 48 applications at first. The MK_DEBUG decline log (every `return false` of the matcher labelled)
+showed the pattern walk succeeding on 47 and the final check declining them all for *overlap*: ggml-alloc places the
+rotated Q over the Q projection (dead after the clip in the unfused graph), either at the same address or 0.5-9 KB
+below it, and the fused kernel reads the projection while it writes the rotated Q (different blocks, no ordering).
+Fix in the model graph, not the kernel: when `LLAMA_INKLING_MK_QKV` is set, `build_inkling2` marks the Q projection
+`ggml_set_output`, which the allocator never frees or reuses (12 KB per application, 576 KB per graph). The kernel
+keeps its overlap check as a guard. The one remaining decline (`q rotation`, node 1103) is one application whose
+next node after the Q clip is not the rotation; 47 of 48 fuse.
+
+| config (two runs each) | short-1 | short-2 | 54K |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| rec+woq | 103.8 / 103.4 | 103.7 / 102.6 | 80.4 / 79.9 |
+| rec+woq+qkv | 109.0 / 108.6 | 108.5 / 108.6 | 83.2 / 83.0 |
+
+QKV: +5% short, +3.5% at 54K; 14 launches per application saved (672 per token).
+
+Recommended production set now: `LLAMA_INKLING_MK_GLUE=1 LLAMA_INKLING_MK_RELTAB=1 LLAMA_INKLING_MK_MOESCALE=1
+LLAMA_INKLING_GEMV=1 LLAMA_INKLING_MK_PROJ=1 LLAMA_INKLING_NO_MASK=1 LLAMA_INKLING_MK_WOQ=1 LLAMA_INKLING_MK_QKV=1`
+(each bit-identical to the unfused graph; MK_CHECK 0 with all of them). Remaining barrier-free candidates: SITU
+emitting the down product's q8_1 (the hand-off must carry 8 rows), the R clip + tau, the 48th QKV application.
